The  command  displays  or sets various audio system mixing vari‐
ables.  If a list of variables is present on  the  command  line,
then  prints  the current value of those variables for the speci‐
fied device.  If the flag is specified, all variables for the de‐
vice are printed.  If the flag is specified, attempts to set  the
specified variables to the given values.  The flag can be used to
give  an  alternative mixer device.  The default is The flag sup‐
presses printing of the variable name.  The flag shows the possi‐
ble values of enumeration and set valued  variables.   Enumerated
values  are  shown  in brackets and set values are shown in curly
braces The exact set of controls that can be manipulated  depends
